{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And they journeyed from Mount Hor to go around the land of Edom, etc.</b> And it is written: ״ותקצר נפש העם״ — when they saw that they were turning backward toward the way of the wilderness, it was hard in their eyes like death, for they thought to enter the land of Israel immediately and eat of the produce of the land, and now they were returning to a place where water and food are not to be found there. And if you ask: what complaint is there here — behold they had the manna? For this it is written: ״ונפשנו קצה בלחם הקלקל״. One who sees and tastes is not like one who tastes without seeing — because he does not see the substance of the thing that he is tasting, and it is not considered in his eyes as anything. Or alternatively: they did not experience that good flavor unless they toiled over it — grinding it in millstones or pounding it in a mortar. And so the verse in the portion of בהעלותך implies, which writes concerning it: ״והיה טעמו כטעם לשד השמן״."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:43.377338445Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}